% 48s-self-hosting-driver.weft — Stage 8t: the compilation driver, written in
% C, compiled by kcc itself, and linked back into the compiler.

\chapter{Self-Hosting: The Compilation Driver in C}
\label{ch:self-hosting-driver}

The driver of Chapter~\ref{ch:compile-driver} is the compiler's outer shell: it
runs every phase in order for one file, loops that over many under \texttt{-c},
and---invoked without \texttt{-c}---compiles and then links an executable by
running the system assembler and linker as child processes.  Porting it puts the
orchestration itself through kcc-compiled C: the argument parsing, the
straight-line pipeline, the fork/exec spawning, and the linker command line.
Every compilation the code-generation suite runs and every executable the
end-to-end suite links passes through this file, so a green sweep of both is the
witness.

\section{State, Strings, and the Pipeline}

The port owns the two driver globals (the captured environment and the
\texttt{--emit-asm} flag) and declares as externs the target/debug flags other
modules own, the whole phase pipeline, and the syscalls used to spawn processes.
The command-line option spellings and the assembler/linker paths are string
constants---compared against arguments and passed as \texttt{argv} elements.
\texttt{kcc\_driver\_compile} is the sequential pipeline: read the source, run
the phases to optimized IR, then either dispatch to the x86 back end or generate
ARM64 code and write the Mach-O object.

@l c
@d Selfhost: driver preamble @{
void *kcc_arena_alloc(long size);
void *kcc_memcpy(void *dst, const void *src, unsigned long n);
int kcc_memcmp(const void *a, const void *b, unsigned long n);
unsigned long kcc_strlen(const char *s);
int kcc_strcmp(const char *a, const char *b);
void kcc_io_flush(void);
void kcc_io_err(const char *s);

void kcc_source_open(const char *path);
void kcc_source_encode(void);
void kcc_source_splice(void);
void kcc_lex_init(void *base, unsigned long size);
void kcc_pp_init(void);
void kcc_pp_force_include(const char *path);
void kcc_strtab_init(void);
void kcc_typedef_init(void);
void *kcc_parse(void);
void kcc_types_init(void);
void kcc_symtab_init(void);
